title: "Noise-Referenced Stability Feature Selection"
authors:
  - family-names: "Winiski"
    given-names: "Jake"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20358454
url: "https://github.com/JakeWiniski/Noise-Referenced-Stability-Feature-Selection"
date-released: 2026-05-23
version: "0.1.0"
license: "Apache-2.0"
abstract: >-
  Initial proof-of-concept release of Noise-Referenced Stability Feature
  Selection, a practical workflow for identifying reliable predictors in
  noisy, small-to-moderate experimental datasets where interpretability
  matters. The workflow combines bootstrap resampling, Random Forest
  permutation importance, and an explicit shuffled-target noise baseline
  to distinguish stable signal from spurious association.
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - stability selection
  - permutation importance
  - noise baseline
  - bootstrap
  - machine learning
  - experimental data
  - process analytics
  - interpretable machine learning
  - statistical learning
